functor: 1
title: box
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`box` · enclose · a restricted or boxed version.

# Form

`x.box` on a symbol, `(a + b).box` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `plus.box` | $plus.box$ | font glyph U+229E |
| `theta.hat.box` | $theta.hat.box$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A restricted or boxed version. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A shape around the base: a circle, a box or a square. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.

# From LaTeX

`\boxplus` becomes `plus.box`, `\boxed{x}` becomes `(x).box`.

